From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jean-Baptiste Leonesio <jbleonesio@squey.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:49:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] QMainWindowLayout: allocate the platform drag on the heap

QDragManager::drag() deletes the QDrag with deleteLater() once the drag
is over, and on Wayland QWaylandDrag::cancel() and finishDrag() do it
from inside the drag event loop. performPlatformWidgetDrag() built its
QDrag on the stack, although QDrag must be constructed on the heap: when
the drag event loop processed the deferred delete before exec()
returned, the drag of a dock widget deleted a stack object, and glibc
aborted with "double free or corruption (out)" or the process crashed.

Qt 6.9 and 6.10.0 to 6.10.1 get there when Escape, or a mouse release
that no drop target accepts, cancels the drag:
QWaylandDisplay::flushRequests() delivers that event at the start of a
loop iteration, before the posted events of the same iteration. Qt
6.10.2 no longer flushes the window system events there (qtbase
44b6b62d83), which hides this ordering, but the QDrag still lives on the
stack.
---
 qtbase/src/widgets/widgets/qmainwindowlayout.cpp | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/qtbase/src/widgets/widgets/qmainwindowlayout.cpp b/qtbase/src/widgets/widgets/qmainwindowlayout.cpp
index 02e2889..97ba28b 100644
--- a/qtbase/src/widgets/widgets/qmainwindowlayout.cpp
+++ b/qtbase/src/widgets/widgets/qmainwindowlayout.cpp
@@ -3449,7 +3449,9 @@ Qt::DropAction QMainWindowLayout::performPlatformWidgetDrag(QLayoutItem *widgetI
 {
     draggingWidget = widgetItem;
     QWidget *widget = widgetItem->widget();
-    auto drag = QDrag(widget);
+    // The drag manager, or the platform drag that owns it, calls deleteLater() on the drag,
+    // and the drag event loop can process that deletion before exec() returns.
+    auto drag = new QDrag(widget);
     auto mimeData = new QMimeData();
     auto window = widgetItem->widget()->windowHandle();
 
@@ -3462,9 +3464,9 @@ Qt::DropAction QMainWindowLayout::performPlatformWidgetDrag(QLayoutItem *widgetI
     mimeData->setData("application/x-qt-mainwindowdrag-window"_L1,
                       serialize(reinterpret_cast<qintptr>(window)));
     mimeData->setData("application/x-qt-mainwindowdrag-position"_L1, serialize(pressPosition));
-    drag.setMimeData(mimeData);
+    drag->setMimeData(mimeData);
 
-    auto result = drag.exec();
+    auto result = drag->exec();
 
     draggingWidget = nullptr;
     return result;
-- 
